{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "title": "s2_11_g0_5_pre_authorization@6.0.0",
  "description": "Deterministic S2.11 / G0.5 pre-authorization user decision capsule v6. v6 supersedes the v3/v4/v5 current-state/active-binding judgments; every v3/v4/v5 core asset stays byte-exact, anchored to its FIXED ORIGIN COMMIT (31ac757d… / 8e8b488e… / 7883739…; hardcoded SHA-256 map in src/bpc_hybrid/capsule_lifecycle.py, independent of HEAD). v5's full audit WAS green (final receipt 2118 passed / 24 skipped / 19 warnings in 941.91s) and v5 is NOT a red checkpoint, but v5's caller-supplied validation-result protection was overturned by v6 counterexamples: classify_frozen now has NO validation-result parameter and re-verifies the draft/frozen configs, the authorization manifest, the append-only authorization event and the prior-results evidence scan from disk on every call; prior results are derived from disk evidence (never a caller bool); the authorization manifest must fully bind the approved scope/sentence/event/checkpoint. v6 also adds adapter formal_evidence_provenance (re-verified evidence context, controlled scope enums, resolved-path containment). G0.5 stays draft_not_frozen (raw-byte hash domain 61938c99…; 51a6e4fe… never an authorization hash); G4 remains dry-run; nothing is applied.",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "report_id",
    "build_note",
    "v5_audit_facts",
    "fixed_origin_anchors",
    "supersedes",
    "state_matrix",
    "license_audit",
    "mapping_options",
    "human_gold_protocol",
    "g0_5_candidate",
    "g0_5_promotion_readiness",
